.TH PYQOA 1 "2026-09-08" "PyQOA 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pyqoa \- desktop chat client for OpenAI-compatible APIs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyqoa
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PyQOA
is a PyQt6 desktop client for any OpenAI-compatible endpoint: the OpenAI cloud, a
local Ollama server, OpenRouter, or a custom gateway. Conversations are stored
locally in SQLite and can be searched full-text, branched, exported and backed up.
.PP
Replies stream with live Markdown rendering and syntax-highlighted code. The client
supports named provider profiles, tool calling over built-ins and MCP servers, image
and file attachments, per-chat model overrides, token and cost tracking, and
light/dark theming.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
as the profile directory (settings, database and vector store) instead of the
default location.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Activate the named provider profile on startup.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-chat
Start in a fresh chat instead of reopening the most recent one.
.TP
.BI \-\-prompt " TEXT"
Open a new chat and send
.I TEXT
immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-selftest
Run a headless check of the bundled feature surface (Qt, Markdown rendering, icon,
database and full-text search, PDF export, token counting, keyring, vector memory)
and exit non-zero if a required check failed. Useful for verifying a packaged build.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pyqoa/settings.json
Configuration, including provider profiles. API keys are stored here in plain text
unless the OS keyring option is enabled.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pyqoa/chats.db
SQLite database of chats, messages and attachments.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pyqoa/vector_memory/
Chroma vector store, only when vector memory is enabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin. Set to
.B offscreen
to run without a display, as
.B \-\-selftest
does automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch straight into a local Ollama profile:
.PP
.RS
.B pyqoa \-\-profile Ollama
.RE
.PP
Ask a one-off question in a new chat:
.PP
.RS
.B pyqoa \-\-prompt "explain SQLite WAL mode"
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/pyqoa/README.md .
